.Dd November 14, 2026
.Dt NOQTIS-UNBOX 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm noqtis-unbox
.Nd open a file sealed with noqtis box
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm noqtis unbox
.Fl k Ar key
.Fl o Ar out
.Op Fl c Ar ctx
.Op Fl -pass-fd Ar n | Fl -pass-env Ar name
.Op Fl f | Fl -force
.Ar file
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm noqtis unbox
decrypts what
.Xr noqtis-box 1
wrote,
.Ar file
or standard input for
.Ar - ,
with the ML-KEM secret key in
.Ar key ,
to
.Ar out
(created owner-only, mode 0600) or standard output for
.Ar - .
Each chunk is written only after its tag has verified.
When a chunk does not verify (the file was changed, cut, reordered or
lengthened, or is not for this key or context), the command stops with
exit status 2 and removes
.Ar out ;
on standard output, what was written had verified but the data is cut
short, so check the exit status before using it.
A header that names a chunk size outside 1024 to 16777216 bytes is
refused before anything is allocated.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl k Ar key , Fl -key Ns = Ns Ar key
The ML-KEM secret key file.
.It Fl o Ar out , Fl -out Ns = Ns Ar out
The output file, or
.Ar - .
.It Fl c Ar ctx , Fl -ctx Ns = Ns Ar ctx
The context string given to
.Xr noqtis-box 1 .
.It Fl -pass-fd Ar n , Fl -pass-env Ar name
The passphrase of a protected key, as in
.Xr noqtis-dec 1 .
.It Fl f , Fl -force
Replace an existing output file.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 when every chunk verified; 2 otherwise, or on a usage, key or file
error.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-box 1 ,
.Xr nqkfeini 3
